{"data": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2114092072550670336"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:30:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114092125080146143"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/qNJDx7vioK", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114092125080146143/video/1", "media_key": "13_2114092072550670336", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/qNJDx7vioK"}]}, "id": "2114092125080146143", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 5956, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "1/3 Growth in Latin America and the Caribbean remains resilient, projected at 2.3% in 2026, 2.5% in 2027, and 2.9% in 2028. Strong U.S. demand, high commodity prices, favorable financial conditions, tourism, and remittances are offsetting trade and geopolitical pressures. https://t.co/qNJDx7vioK", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114092125080146143"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-24T19:06:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114071006633501034"], "id": "2114071006633501034", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 16852, "like_count": 75, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "Markets continued to revisit this past week the previously comforting assumptions around tech ROI and funding needs, triggering NASDAQ market weakness and a flight to quality, even as confidence in the sector’s long-term economic growth effects remains broadly intact.\nLooking", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114071006633501034"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114046768258359297"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:30:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114046770531663926"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "What happens when grocery and utility bills soar? This talk explore...", "display_url": "youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH…", "end": 230, "expanded_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH7KvWY", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113729750674145280/C6ZatK0m?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113729750674145280/C6ZatK0m?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 207, "status": 200, "title": "Analytical Corner: Navigating a Shock-Prone World: Lessons from Cost-of-Living Crises", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH7KvWY", "url": "https://t.co/iHRM8fTtiI"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Pr7IjqbkMK", "end": 254, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114046770531663926/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114046768258359297", "start": 231, "url": "https://t.co/Pr7IjqbkMK"}]}, "id": "2114046770531663926", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 11666, "like_count": 37, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "When grocery and utility bills soar, the burden is not shared equally. This Analytical Corner explores who is most affected, why the distributional consequences matter, and how policy can make a difference: https://t.co/iHRM8fTtiI https://t.co/Pr7IjqbkMK", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114046770531663926"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:13:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114042558074806389"], "id": "2114042558074806389", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1253, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Don't abliterate and drive", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2114042558074806389"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114030311554052097"]}, "author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:41:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114034453131764202"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/x0S3eJFCCl", "end": 90, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114034453131764202/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114030311554052097", "start": 67, "url": "https://t.co/x0S3eJFCCl"}]}, "id": "2114034453131764202", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 9316, "like_count": 50, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "A college student reacts to some of what is written by Econvitals. https://t.co/x0S3eJFCCl", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114034453131764202"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114032500313915392", "3_2114032500280266752"]}, "author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:33:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114032505305354626"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 149, "start": 145, "tag": "qpr"}], "mentions": [{"end": 154, "id": "71210107", "start": 150, "username": "QPR"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/VwXoAr7XSx", "end": 178, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114032505305354626/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114032500313915392", "start": 155, "url": "https://t.co/VwXoAr7XSx"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/VwXoAr7XSx", "end": 178, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114032505305354626/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114032500280266752", "start": 155, "url": "https://t.co/VwXoAr7XSx"}]}, "id": "2114032505305354626", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 18399, "like_count": 90, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "A decisive win like this doesn’t happen often for QPR—or any team I support, for that matter. \nI'm currently alternating between shock and joy! \n#qpr @QPR https://t.co/VwXoAr7XSx", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114032505305354626"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113655574122438656"]}, "author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114031666587168877"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 32, "start": 24, "tag": "BLSdata"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Bureau of Labor Statistics is the principal fact-finding agency for the Federal Government in the broad field of labor economics and statistics.", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/update.htm", "end": 98, "expanded_url": "https://bls.gov/opub/update.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111846596279402496/98Bnf4uL?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111846596279402496/98Bnf4uL?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 75, "status": 200, "title": "U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/", "url": "https://t.co/6g1gI94GS0"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/wdThC30hcH", "end": 122, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2114031666587168877/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113655574122438656", "start": 99, "url": "https://t.co/wdThC30hcH"}]}, "id": "2114031666587168877", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1855, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Catch up on all the new #BLSdata and publications that came out this week! https://t.co/6g1gI94GS0 https://t.co/wdThC30hcH", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2114031666587168877"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:10:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114026870098518060"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/AISecurityInst…", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AISecurityInst/status/2113626762617741389?s=20", "start": 256, "url": "https://t.co/FCIpX5tdUR"}]}, "id": "2114026870098518060", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 1941, "like_count": 30, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113626762617741389", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I'm glad Ant and AISI dug deeper here, though for the record, it already seemed in July like Anthropic's defense of Mythos's behavior was rushed + that motivated reasoning was prob at work\n\nAlso, Astra being v. bad here too is an important finding as well https://t.co/FCIpX5tdUR", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2114026870098518060"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:38:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114003560723534156"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A note from the site's launch: what a company would have needed to build Econvitals with every line of code written by people.", "display_url": "econvitals.org/about/before-a…", "end": 246, "expanded_url": "https://econvitals.org/about/before-ai/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114003562518781952/_nAeYfCI?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114003562518781952/_nAeYfCI?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 223, "status": 200, "title": "What would it have taken to build Econvitals before AI? — Econvitals", "unwound_url": "https://econvitals.org/about/before-ai/", "url": "https://t.co/eu9k5HxEHo"}]}, "id": "2114003560723534156", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 49, "impression_count": 27569, "like_count": 120, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "I asked Claude how much it would have taken to develop Econvitals pre-coding agents. It's answer: a team of about 50 people working for three years with a budget of $20 million.\n\nIs this correct or too high? I'm not sure.\n\nhttps://t.co/eu9k5HxEHo", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114003560723534156"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:30:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114001653879672877"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 223, "id": "825088493764407298", "start": 211, "username": "polynoamial"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/andrewcurran_/…", "end": 307, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/andrewcurran_/status/2113717691420950973", "start": 284, "url": "https://t.co/jJiU7pV2iv"}]}, "id": "2114001653879672877", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 51, "impression_count": 23908, "like_count": 312, "quote_count": 12, "reply_count": 157, "retweet_count": 28}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113717691420950973", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Without being overly credulous, we should be taking seemingly “out there” ideas about AI cybersecurity from the Labs more seriously. Examples: Anthropic was mocked for saying Mythos-level AI changed cyber &amp; @polynoamial for saying that models would find novel ways to coordinate. https://t.co/jJiU7pV2iv", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2114001653879672877"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:19:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113998856669016457"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 37, "id": "2592325153", "start": 24, "username": "Claudia_Sahm"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/Claudia_Sahm/s…", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Claudia_Sahm/status/2113948073671921972", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/lM3dcySv7G"}]}, "id": "2113998856669016457", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 36, "impression_count": 26701, "like_count": 113, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 8}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113948073671921972", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I mostly agree with you @Claudia_Sahm.\n\nI expect colleagues to continue to have research assistants even if only for mentorship than because they need the help.\n\nCompanies to have junior staff not because they need their current work but to train them for future roles. https://t.co/lM3dcySv7G", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2113998856669016457"}, {"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-10-24T13:01:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113979122103759273"], "id": "2113979122103759273", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 142, "impression_count": 51815, "like_count": 562, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 69, "retweet_count": 29}, "text": "Symbolic learning works", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2113979122103759273"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113971269096132608"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T12:30:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113971276104740886"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/mMzgpDWo8c", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113971276104740886/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113971269096132608", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/mMzgpDWo8c"}]}, "id": "2113971276104740886", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 28, "impression_count": 41374, "like_count": 235, "quote_count": 11, "reply_count": 20, "retweet_count": 62}, "text": "In emerging market and developing economies, growth is projected to slow to 3.7% in 2026 before recovering to 4.4% in 2027, with prospects shaped by commodity dependence, sensitivity to financial conditions, policy frameworks, and position in the global technology value chain. https://t.co/mMzgpDWo8c", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113971276104740886"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113910870153830400"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T08:30:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113910873320575448"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 227, "id": "1537107694359875584", "start": 217, "username": "STenreyro"}], "urls": [{"description": "Countries must move from coping to rebuilding, restoring fiscal space and supply-side resilience to enhance their ability to grow sustainably", "display_url": "imf.org/en/blogs/artic…", "end": 268, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2026/10/12/global-economic-resilience-is-under-strain-demanding-decisive-policy-action", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112734256007114752/DY3lbY-6?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 2099}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112734256007114752/DY3lbY-6?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 245, "status": 200, "title": "Global Economic Resilience Is Under Strain, Demanding Decisive Policy Action", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2026/10/12/global-economic-resilience-is-under-strain-demanding-decisive-policy-action", "url": "https://t.co/javlPkw7Ks"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/uTpCKLHZwN", "end": 292, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113910873320575448/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113910870153830400", "start": 269, "url": "https://t.co/uTpCKLHZwN"}]}, "id": "2113910873320575448", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 19197, "like_count": 126, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 30}, "text": "The global economy proved resilient through pandemic, war, inflation, and trade tension, but strains are showing. Policymakers must move from coping to rebuilding, and countries should build resilience together. Read @STenreyro’s blog for more. https://t.co/javlPkw7Ks https://t.co/uTpCKLHZwN", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113910873320575448"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113708469681258496"]}, "author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-24T06:00:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113873354578960423"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 226, "id": "29963394", "start": 212, "username": "MilanoFinanza"}], "urls": [{"description": "The European Central Bank (ECB) is the central bank of the European Union countries which have adopted the euro. Our main task is to maintain price stability in the euro area and so preserve the purchasing power of the single currency.", "display_url": "link.europa.eu/PFJjgx", "end": 271, "expanded_url": "https://link.europa.eu/PFJjgx", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113873366654259200/8WCZ6V9s?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113873366654259200/8WCZ6V9s?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 248, "status": 200, "title": "Interview with Milano Finanza", "unwound_url": "https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/inter/date/2026/html/ecb.in261024~ee2ba73cf3.en.html", "url": "https://t.co/FC9TvVPpOP"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/7FRB01HBwA", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.