t the biggest driver wasn't growth or fiscal consolidation. It was financial repression. https://t.co/BvlYbPGiUZ https://t.co/t0SY8GKSNz", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113744825623445740"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-23T21:24:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113743316105752832"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/econvitals/sta…", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/econvitals/status/2113738508959358989", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/089tqvebN9"}]}, "id": "2113743316105752832", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 13013, "like_count": 70, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 7}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113738508959358989", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Looks like we'll see very strong growth for Q3 GDP, data out on Thursday.\n\nEconvitals Composite tracking is for GDP growth of 3.2% in Q3.\n\nThe composite tracker is a weighted average of several other measures--including Econvitals own estimate (2.4%).\n\nPrivate demand *much* https://t.co/089tqvebN9", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2113743316105752832"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113729679127719936"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:30:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113729745636741327"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "What happens when grocery and utility bills soar? This talk explore...", "display_url": "youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH…", "end": 255, "expanded_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH7KvWY", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113729750674145280/C6ZatK0m?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113729750674145280/C6ZatK0m?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 232, "status": 200, "title": "Analytical Corner: Navigating a Shock-Prone World: Lessons from Cost-of-Living Crises", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH7KvWY", "url": "https://t.co/iHRM8fTtiI"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/xVy8Oc9Xzx", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113729745636741327/video/1", "media_key": "13_2113729679127719936", "start": 256, "url": "https://t.co/xVy8Oc9Xzx"}]}, "id": "2113729745636741327", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 17, "impression_count": 19066, "like_count": 77, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "When grocery and energy bills soar, how can governments best protect the vulnerable? Keeping prices down for everyone is costly and often benefits wealthier households. In this Analytical Corner, Chiara Maggi explains a better way: https://t.co/iHRM8fTtiI https://t.co/xVy8Oc9Xzx", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113729745636741327"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113724902306115584"]}, "author_id": "825088493764407298", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:28:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113729267418956201"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/MHH9kxLN3G", "end": 231, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2113729267418956201/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113724902306115584", "start": 208, "url": "https://t.co/MHH9kxLN3G"}, {"display_url": "x.com/Eric_Wallace_/…", "end": 255, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Eric_Wallace_/status/2113718905562862065", "start": 232, "url": "https://t.co/zuTByFSQuy"}]}, "id": "2113729267418956201", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 253, "impression_count": 58618, "like_count": 1638, "quote_count": 19, "reply_count": 82, "retweet_count": 118}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113718905562862065", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Last month a large team of agents used over 100 billion tokens to resolve the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize problem. Now we're using a similar approach for red-teaming to find and fix infra vulnerabilities. https://t.co/MHH9kxLN3G https://t.co/zuTByFSQuy", "url": "https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2113729267418956201"}, {"author_id": "26538229